Full legal text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/legalcode
Human-readable summary: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/

In short, you are free to:

  - Read it, learn from it, and share links to it.
  - Quote short excerpts with clear attribution back to
    https://www.backendengineer.in and the original page.

You may NOT, without explicit written permission:

  - Republish, rehost, or redistribute the lesson text itself, in whole or in
    reworded/derivative form, on another site, in a course, a book, a
    newsletter, or any other product.
  - Use the content for any commercial purpose.
  - Train a model on this content, or use it to generate derivative content,
    without permission.

This license applies only to the written lesson content in `src/content/`.
The code that renders it - components, the MDX pipeline, visuals, styling,
and everything else in this repository - is MIT-licensed; see the `LICENSE`
file at the repository root.

